            "text": "A total solar eclipse is visible everywhere on Earth's sunlit side at the same time."
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "A solar eclipse occurs whenever the Moon is on the Sun-facing side of Earth, even if it is not lined up to cast a shadow on Earth."
